 "about": "Reference values for the tests of the viewer (tests/unit/v2-*.test.mjs, tests/e2e/v2-*.spec.mjs): the sky around the target of seven frames, the three of tests/fixtures/frames and the four of tests/fixtures/showcase/barnard-d5. Made on 14 November 2026 with astropy from the IMAGE header of each frame (bytes 0 to 28799 of the file: recorded in tests/fixtures/frames for three frames, read from the bucket nasa-irsa-spherex for the other four). For each frame: sky is the position of the target pixel (all_pix2world, distortion terms included) and cd is [east per x, east per y, north per x, north per y] in degrees per pixel on the plane that touches the sky there, from positions half a pixel to each side of the target; north and east are unit vectors in stamp pixels (x right, y up) and north_angle is the angle of north in degrees clockwise from up; pixel_arcsec is the square root of the area of a pixel there; points are five pixels of the stamp (its corners and its middle, 0-based, y counted from the lowest row) with their sky position from all_pix2world and their wavelength and bandwidth in micrometres from the table of the detector in tests/fixtures/wave/tables.json, interpolated with scipy. Checked while it was made: all_world2pix of the target agrees with x0 + tx, y0 + ty of every frame within 0.000001 pixel.",
